    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d915">

                <pb facs="0885" n="787" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg787"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Señor
                            Azpíroz.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic">November 20,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 134.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note No. 153, of the 15th instant, furnishing the Spanish text
                    of the draft of a convention submitted with my note No. 127, of the 31st <pb
                        facs="0886" n="788" xml:id="pg788"/> ultimo, continuing in force and effect
                    for an indefinite period the water boundary convention of March 1, 1889, and the
                    commission established thereunder.</p>
                <p>I have had the two texts prepared for signature and beg to inclose for your
                    inspection the United States and Mexican copies of the convention. If found
                    correct, I shall be pleased to sign the convention with you to-morrow morning at
                    11 o’clock, if you can find it convenient to call at that hour.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
